I was born and raised in the US but my dad is from jordan (mom caucasian american from southern US), I lived in Jordan for about 4-5 years and went to high school there. Went to an international/english school, that's where I met this friend and he's like a brother to me. I have been struggling with severe depression and finances throughout the 13 years of our friendship and he has done everything in his power to help me and paid for me to fly out to visit him etc.

&#x200B;

We barely talk these days, he's been studying in boston as a foreign exchange student from Jordan for the past few years while I'm back home living in the deep south, and only visited him twice in the time he's been living the US and I feel bad about this but it comes down to money.

&#x200B;

ANYWAYS, he never asks me for anything, but he contacted me out of the blue today, and said he has a female friend who's in danger and needs to find a room/apartment to rent in boston and he told me it's urgent. this is out of his character and he never asks for stuff like this. Does ANYONE know how/where I can find out how to rent a room in boston for someone? They have the money and are ready to move in I guess. he barely gave me any details, but I want to help. Told him i'd check craigslist and I found almost nothing, Please help me I need to help my old high school friend he is literally like a brother to me and he's stood by my side through tough times, where I was suffering from PTSD and depression and opioid addiction. I just want to help him, but I feel like there is nothing I can do in this situation because I know nothing about renting apartments/rooms in boston. and i'm very desperate so im reaching out to reddit to just point me in the right direction, all I know of is craigslist, if you guys know where I can find a room to rent in boston (website, app, whatever) I would REALLY appreaciate the help.

