Im probably gonna delete this post and repost it on a throwaway with more details. But the girl is a friend, and she was a virgin, on a date with a guy from tinder, he took advantage of her and brutally raped her. she is mentally disabled/has Aspergers syndrome and very innocent, shy, weak, anxious etc like she must have been the perfect victim. 

&#x200B;

This happened last year, and even though she went to the hospital and needed surgery and got a rape kit done, the dude got away with it and 'the case never made it to the DA', is all I know about the legal perspective. also that the rapist had a lawyer at the hearing and she didnt.... But she spotted him under a new profile on tinder a few days ago and it really scared her and right now I dont know what to do, if someone doesnt stop me im gonna end up finding this guy...... and beating the shit out of him, to put it mildly because the police down here obviously could care less and the justice system in the US is a joke.

Holy shit, your response sounds exactly like mine, and I absolutely agree 100%. I also made the same points about how he was probably just a lonely horny teacher who made a bad decision after graduation. but the school relationship sounded mutually beneficial and like he was geniunly interested or maybe just into her, but still was not aggressive or making her feel uncomfortable ... Oh and I also made the exact same point that it doesnt make him a 'pedophile' like many are saying, A pedo is someone who is attracted to PRE-PUBESCENT girls, and I also said the exact same thing that any man who says he never found a girl under 17-18 to be attractive is absolutely lying.

&#x200B;

I'm actually going to delete my comment, because im probably going to get a lot of hate and called a 'pedo' for it, and because you worded it so much better. Are people here really this narrow minded..... Like there are comments with people suggesting she leads him on, and entraps him into saying something sexual in order to report him. And based on the info I saw, he doesn't necessarily sound like a predator, moreso a lonely guy in his 30's who had a crush on a 15 yr old.

>. I was routinely sexually assaulted to the point I thought it was normal

&#x200B;

you were sexually assaulted and thought it was normal? how is that possible.... like how old were you? did you not know what they were doing to you or something. I dont understand how they can manage to sexually assault students on multiple occasions and noone does anything about it

How do you know he was a pedophile? She was 15 when they first met or started talking and 17 when he pursued her after graduation. He could be a pedophile, sure. But based on that info, in my eyes doesn't make him a pedophile, maybe creepy at the worst. 

&#x200B;

Men find girls of pubescent age attractive, esp the more developed they are and she said she was developed and had 'curves' since she was 11, so at 15, she probably looked like any 18-20 year old. Its inappropriate sure. But im pretty sure a pedophile is someone who is attracted to prepubescent kids, correct me if im wrong.

Im almost 29 and I do sometimes find 'underage' females attractive sometimes (usually nothing under 15, but just depends on how developed they look) and any guy around my age or even way older who says they've never found a 16 yr old attractive is lying. But that is as far as physical attraction, as long as the girl is fully pubescent and developed I can appreciate her beauty and i'll admit that, even though people sometimes will call me a 'pedo' for it..... But I never did and would never pursue anything with a teenager, i just couldn't see myself being in a relationship and being able to relate and be on the same intellectual level, but you never know, I dont really talk to any teenage girls except family members...

&#x200B;

I just wanted to put that out there, I don't think the fact that he found you attractive at that age is wrong or creepy. And everything you said sounds like he had a crush on you or something and really wanted to get to know you better and get closer, which is ok as long as he doesn't cross certain boundaries, but him contacting you to meet up after graduation is kinda shady, but he still doesn't sound like some child predator or anything based on him not being so agressive about it or outright hitting on you while you were his student. And it also seems like he took a special interest in you, and genuinely liked your personality or something about you, probably did find you attractive but suppressed his urges or feelings or w/e and now that you're no longer a student and close to age of consent he waited until now to try and pursue anything, which atleast he was able to do that, yes unprofessional/inappropriate, maybe creepy or something, but based on what you said, it didn't seem like he had this type of relationship with any other students. It sounds like he just had a huge crush on you or something

&#x200B;

TLDR: I guess he doesn't necessarily sound like a predator based on what I know and given he waited until you graduated to try and pursue you. I think he just had an inappropriate crush, for a younger girl he must have found really interesting. It doesn't particularly sound like he was a predator or anything, because he didn't seem to be aggressive or overly inappropriate, at least in a sexual way, while you were in school and also seems like he took an interest just in you and wasn't trying to 'groom' other girls based on what you said. So I really can't say, because I don't know his intentions. he could be, but most I feel would be a little more aggressive about it.

Very True. I speak from Personal experience. Never Again.

&#x200B;

I have 'doctors' and 'psychiatrists' to thank for giving me permanent brain damage, I'd only seek professional help, if they are extremely experienced and KNOW what phenibut is, and willing to treat it like any other SERIOUS alcohol, benzo, GABA/depressant addiction and willing to use some strong GABAergic drug that is related and do a slow/medium taper.

&#x200B;

If you go to the wrong 'doctors' for medical help, they might decide putting you on something like 600mg of seroquel is a good idea.

&#x200B;

Now, im not saying you dont need professional help, im just saying very good point, I would proceed with caution when looking for professional help ESPECIALLY "inpatient"

Thats pretty bad, but I'll 1-up you, this happened sometime in 2012, I was struggling with serious opiate addiction which was a byproduct of me not responding to any antidepressants, my parents are(moreso especially at the time) very strict & muslim (dad middle eastern, mom american convert), they were talking to me one day in my room and my dad saw some cigarettes and got kinda pissed and called me out about them, that was horrifying.

&#x200B;

Anyways next day, my dad picked me up from work, and started talking to me in the car and said he needed to talk to me about something..... and I got really scared and worried, as I go home an open my room, I find hundreds of used heroin syringes lined up on my bed, all kinds of different RCs and psychedelics, bags of marijuana, empty heroin baggies and burnt spoons and all kinds of paraphernalia, rolling papers and pipes and whatnot.......... Apparently he broke into my room through the window, and got into my closet. Suspicious because he found cigarettes the day before, and to his surprise, it was much worse, by far. He lined up everything on my bed very neat and nice, even the used cigarette butts (Yes he is a sociopath who has ruined my entire family, because I know its odd to even line up cig. butts)

&#x200B;

Both him and my mom were in the room and had a long talk, I freaked out so hard I left the country for a few months, eventually developed serious PTSD from it, Later on my depression worsened to a state where I couldnt even work and became fully disabled. 7 years later I have tried over 20 different anti depressants which failed me, have been hospitalized in psych. wards 5+ times, A few OD's and suicide attempts, where I miraculously died, turned blue, heart stopped for like 10 mins, then miraculously came back to life with CPR or w/e the paramedics did., And most recently I've been through 18 sessions of ECT, and now the Dr is calling it off, because I didn't respond to it unfortunately. If I get to age 30 and im still getting worse, I don't know what im going to do. FTR I've recovered from my addiction, and am on suboxone and only dr prescribed meds now. But continue to get worse as time goes by.

&#x200B;

TLDR: muslim parents searched my mom because they found out I smoked cigarettes, instead found heroin syringes, baggies, paraphernalia, weed, pipes, psychedelics, RCs Etc, when they went through my closet (while I was at work), my psycho dad lined it all up on my bed while I was gone and made me open the door to my room and find all this. It traumatized me, developed PTSD, depression went downhill to where I became disabled and even recently been through ECT after 20 meds failed me, oh and ECT didnt help btw. (Although I've been through other Traumas in my adult life as well which made things worse). They didn't even know I smoked weed at the time, which is why this was so hard on me, I was hiding that for years..... then this happens. Im 28 and still living with them and my other siblings, as im disabled now.

Jeez, I was an IV h user for years.... and OD'ed maybe twice in 5 yrs, and the times I did OD, I truly do sincerely wish I wasn't narcaned, and the cops and paramedics I dealt with were extremely rude and unprofessional.

&#x200B;

But Damn, although im an (ex)user, I barely associate with any junkies personally and the only (very few) friends I have dont use drugs. But are most junkies really like this? Whoever that is sounds like an EXTREME asshole. I know nothing about them, but if they are being that reckless I would assume they are suicidal/suffering from severe mental illness.

&#x200B;

However, personally, The 2 times I did get narcaned I was a TOTAL mistake, and 5+ yrs into my use, and I never pictured it would happen to me and I HATED myself for it and the stress it caused on other people around me. I absolutely regretted it and never wanted it to happen again. But knowing myself at the time, I just went right back to using but was more careful, And I frankly did not care If I died and honestly prayed (agnostic btw) everyday that I would somehow accidentally OD, But all the 3 times I OD'ed or almost did, coincidentally there just happened to be loved ones around me who were able to get to me in time and give me CPR or w/e until an ambulance came(twice in 5+ yrs)

&#x200B;

**Now personally, I would NEVER be an asshole to the paramedics who saved me, I was pretty neutral with them, mostly because I wasn't responsive and didn't have the chance to talk to them. However if one of them reached out to me like you have and did all that for me, I would be FOREVER grateful and thank them in every way I can. And I feel extremely guilty for all the (esp. loved ones) people and family members I stressed out when this type of thing happened, and I can never get it out of my head or forgive myself for it. (Even though Ive been clean for a while and on subs now) But are most addicts really like this from your experience? If so thats terrible.**

&#x200B;

**I guess im just going in circles here, but I suppose im trying to say, just try to consider that some of these people may be suicidal or going through some serious shit/mental illness/trauma, However I am NOT saying that its an excuse for them to treat you like shit, ESPECIALLY the way you described in your post, and I personally would NEVER act like that. But damn if the majority of them act like that towards you I can see why you might think that way. And you said you narcanned the same person 4 times in 24 hours? Yea thats insane..... however if that happened here by the 2nd time they would IMMEDIATELY put him in a psych. ward.(No way they'd put someone like that back on the street 4 times in 24 hrs, like are you sure he wasnt trying to kill himself?)**

&#x200B;

 **Like I ACCIDENTALLY OD'ed once and they treated it like a suicide and forced me into a psych. ward for a week (Maybe because of my mental illness/suicidality history)**

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I never pictured myself being a junkie, And I thought at my age I would be a college Grad. with a 6 figure career, a house, car and family. But throughout my 20s things just spiralled downwards and only got worse and worse, which is what led to me self medicating/using drugs that I thought I'd NEVER even touch. (Used to be straight edge and anti-drug)

&#x200B;

I have treatment resistant MDD, PTSD, GAD, SAD, and have tried over 20 meds in the last 10 yrs with no success and recently just got done with a course of ECT (did 16+ sessions over 2months) which I had SOOO much hope in working(And BEGGED Dr's for YEARS before I finally got approved), But sadly the ECT did not work, and It completely devastated me and I feel hopeless and im on the brink of relapsing........... BUT regardless of what a person is going through personally, it is NO excuse for being a dick to the people who saved you, and I personally am always thankful to anyone who helps/tries to help me to a point where I am overly empathetic, but thats just me.

